    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "270 4  Definition of servitude",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, servitude is the condition of a\nperson (the victim) who provides labour or services, if, because of\nthe use of coercion, threat or deception:\n\n(a) a reasonable person in the position of the victim would not\nconsider himself or herself to be free:\n\n(i) to cease providing the labour or services; or\n\n(ii) to leave the place or area where the victim provides the\nlabour or services; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Criminal Code amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, servitude is the condition of a\nperson (the victim) who provides labour or services, if, because of\nthe use of coercion, threat or deception:\n\n(a) a reasonable person in the position of the victim would not\nconsider himself or herself to be free:\n\n(i) to cease providing the labour or services; or\n\n(ii) to leave the place or area where the victim provides the\nlabour or services; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Criminal Code amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2-logic-diffusion-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2-logic-cogai-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2-logic-shacl-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "21aa82c9205350f78c7021a78f78641aa4813f808366f6cbfe79a9ce3453da6e",
      "skos:note": "A person providing labour or services under coercion, threat, or deception is not considered free."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "270 4  Definition of servitude",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, servitude is the condition of a\nperson (the victim) who provides labour or services, if, because of\nthe use of coercion, threat or deception:\n\n(a) a reasonable person in the position of the victim would not\nconsider himself or herself to be free:\n\n(i) to cease providing the labour or services; or\n\n(ii) to leave the place or area where the victim provides the\nlabour or services; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Criminal Code amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to provide labour or services under coercion, threat, or deception.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The victim is not considered free.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "A reasonable person would not consider themselves free."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal interval of coercion, threat, or deception overlaps with the temporal interval of providing labour or services.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The use of coercion, threat, or deception occurs during the provision of labour or services.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The temporal intervals overlap."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2-logic-diffusion-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Diffuses",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Coercion, threat, or deception diffuses to other persons providing labour or services.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The victim is not considered free.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Other persons are also affected."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2-logic-cogai-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recognizes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The system recognizes the obligation to provide labour or services under coercion, threat, or deception.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The victim provides labour or services.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The system acknowledges the obligation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-2-logic-shacl-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:SHACL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Validates",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The SHACL validation rule checks for the presence of coercion, threat, or deception in providing labour or services.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::shacl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The victim provides labour or services.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The validation rule is satisfied."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-6-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-6-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(b) the victim is significantly deprived of personal freedom in\nrespect of aspects of his or her life other than the provision of\nthe labour or services.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the coercion, threat or deception is\nused against the victim or another person.\n\n(3) The victim may be in a condition of servitude whether or not:\n\n(a) escape from the condition is practically possible for the\nvictim; or\n\n(b) the victim has attempted to escape from the condition.",
      "skos:definition": "(b) the victim is significantly deprived of personal freedom in\nrespect of aspects of his or her life other than the provision of\nthe labour or services.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the coercion, threat or deception is\nused against the victim or another person.\n\n(3) The victim may be in a condition of servitude whether or not:\n\n(a) escape from the condition is practically possible for the\nvictim; or\n\n(b) the victim has attempted to escape from the condition.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-6-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-6-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6f4eb5b967de675706fb216a48764f1dd8f44488c07b6b2756d3b5eba24e0808"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-6-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(b) the victim is significantly deprived of personal freedom in\nrespect of aspects of his or her life other than the provision of\nthe labour or services.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the coercion, threat or deception is\nused against the victim or another person.\n\n(3) The victim may be in a condition of servitude whether or not:\n\n(a) escape from the condition is practically possible for the\nvictim; or\n\n(b) the victim has attempted to escape from the condition."
    },
