    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "270 5  Servitude offences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "Causing a person to enter into or remain in servitude\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the conduct causes another person to enter into or remain in\nservitude.\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 20 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 15 years.\nConducting a business involving servitude\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person conducts any business; and\n\n(b) the business involves the servitude of another person (or\npersons).\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 20 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 15 years.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nCriminal Code amendments  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act",
      "skos:definition": "Causing a person to enter into or remain in servitude\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the conduct causes another person to enter into or remain in\nservitude.\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 20 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 15 years.\nConducting a business involving servitude\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person conducts any business; and\n\n(b) the business involves the servitude of another person (or\npersons).\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 20 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 15 years.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nCriminal Code amendments  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-3-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-3-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "376fe2186077636f93956000ae320b4fb1c388d3b2fecfd67fb554c71b894666"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "270 5  Servitude offences",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "Causing a person to enter into or remain in servitude\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the conduct causes another person to enter into or remain in\nservitude.\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 20 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 15 years.\nConducting a business involving servitude\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person conducts any business; and\n\n(b) the business involves the servitude of another person (or\npersons).\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 20 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 15 years.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nCriminal Code amendments  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act"
    },
