    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "270 6  Definition of forced labour",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, forced labour is the condition of\na person (the victim) who provides labour or services if, because of\nthe use of coercion, threat or deception, a reasonable person in the\nposition of the victim would not consider himself or herself to be\nfree:\n\n(a) to cease providing the labour or services; or\n\n(b) to leave the place or area where the victim provides the\nlabour or services.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the coercion, threat or deception is\nused against the victim or another person.\n\n(3) The victim may be in a condition of forced labour whether or not:\n\n(a) escape from the condition is practically possible for the\nvictim; or\n\n(b) the victim has attempted to escape from the condition.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Criminal Code amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, forced labour is the condition of\na person (the victim) who provides labour or services if, because of\nthe use of coercion, threat or deception, a reasonable person in the\nposition of the victim would not consider himself or herself to be\nfree:\n\n(a) to cease providing the labour or services; or\n\n(b) to leave the place or area where the victim provides the\nlabour or services.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the coercion, threat or deception is\nused against the victim or another person.\n\n(3) The victim may be in a condition of forced labour whether or not:\n\n(a) escape from the condition is practically possible for the\nvictim; or\n\n(b) the victim has attempted to escape from the condition.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Criminal Code amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-4-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-4-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-4-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5a5ee3e75630ad1125e9cebdd4cd3955efa696112ccd5a56f069da5dd35685b8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "270 6  Definition of forced labour",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, forced labour is the condition of\na person (the victim) who provides labour or services if, because of\nthe use of coercion, threat or deception, a reasonable person in the\nposition of the victim would not consider himself or herself to be\nfree:\n\n(a) to cease providing the labour or services; or\n\n(b) to leave the place or area where the victim provides the\nlabour or services.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether the coercion, threat or deception is\nused against the victim or another person.\n\n(3) The victim may be in a condition of forced labour whether or not:\n\n(a) escape from the condition is practically possible for the\nvictim; or\n\n(b) the victim has attempted to escape from the condition.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Criminal Code amendments"
    },
