    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "270 6A  Forced labour offences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "Causing a person to enter into or remain in forced labour\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the conduct causes another person to enter into or remain in\nforced labour.\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 12 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 9 years.\nConducting a business involving forced labour\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person conducts any business; and\n\n(b) the business involves the forced labour of another person (or\npersons).\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 12 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 9 years.\nNote:\nOn a trial for an offence against section 270.5 (servitude offences), the\ntrier of fact may find a defendant not guilty of that offence but guilty\nof the corresponding offence under this section (see subsections",
      "skos:definition": "Causing a person to enter into or remain in forced labour\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the conduct causes another person to enter into or remain in\nforced labour.\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 12 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 9 years.\nConducting a business involving forced labour\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person conducts any business; and\n\n(b) the business involves the forced labour of another person (or\npersons).\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 12 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 9 years.\nNote:\nOn a trial for an offence against section 270.5 (servitude offences), the\ntrier of fact may find a defendant not guilty of that offence but guilty\nof the corresponding offence under this section (see subsections",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-5-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-5-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3368f2ee1b68bd6b27293a6feab1a9eb3e174b1f04f3f847c72abe813ca3e529"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "270 6A  Forced labour offences",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "Causing a person to enter into or remain in forced labour\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the conduct causes another person to enter into or remain in\nforced labour.\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 12 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 9 years.\nConducting a business involving forced labour\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person conducts any business; and\n\n(b) the business involves the forced labour of another person (or\npersons).\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 12 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 9 years.\nNote:\nOn a trial for an offence against section 270.5 (servitude offences), the\ntrier of fact may find a defendant not guilty of that offence but guilty\nof the corresponding offence under this section (see subsections"
    },
