        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-5-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eb3b00b2eb6890d58859a69e3c59150bcf7e27033711407bdfbe70ed4893be5d",
      "skos:note": "Forced labour of another person (or persons) is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-5-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "270(2) 6A  Forced labour offences",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person conducts any business; and\n\n(b) the business involves the forced labour of another person (or\npersons).\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 12 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 9 years.\nNote:\nOn a trial for an offence against section 270.5 (servitude offences), the\ntrier of fact may find a defendant not guilty of that offence but guilty\nof the corresponding offence under this section (see subsections"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-5-ss-2-norm",
