    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "270 7  Deceptive recruiting for labour or services",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "A person (the recruiter) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the recruiter engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the recruiter engages in the conduct with the intention of\ninducing another person (the victim) to enter into an\nengagement to provide labour or services; and\n\n(c) the conduct causes the victim to be deceived about:\n\n(i) the extent to which the victim will be free to leave the\nplace or area where the victim provides the labour or\nservices; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nCriminal Code amendments  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act",
      "skos:definition": "A person (the recruiter) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the recruiter engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the recruiter engages in the conduct with the intention of\ninducing another person (the victim) to enter into an\nengagement to provide labour or services; and\n\n(c) the conduct causes the victim to be deceived about:\n\n(i) the extent to which the victim will be free to leave the\nplace or area where the victim provides the labour or\nservices; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nCriminal Code amendments  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ef5f884f62dc7ed3e49eaae22abc1664a091cd02582c9d48d2aad46995122cc4",
      "skos:note": "Deceptive recruiting for labour or services is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "270 7  Deceptive recruiting for labour or services",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "A person (the recruiter) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the recruiter engages in conduct; and\n\n(b) the recruiter engages in the conduct with the intention of\ninducing another person (the victim) to enter into an\nengagement to provide labour or services; and\n\n(c) the conduct causes the victim to be deceived about:\n\n(i) the extent to which the victim will be free to leave the\nplace or area where the victim provides the labour or\nservices; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nCriminal Code amendments  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-7-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-7"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-7-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies the provision as a prohibition.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2013 No. 6, 2013            9",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-2013-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(ii) the extent to which the victim will be free to cease\nproviding the labour or services; or\n\n(iii) the extent to which the victim will be free to leave his or\nher place of residence; or\n\n(iv) if there is or will be a debt owed or claimed to be owed\nby the victim in connection with the engagement—the\nquantum, or the existence, of the debt owed or claimed\nto be owed; or\n\n(v) the fact that the engagement will involve exploitation,\nor the confiscation of the victim’s travel or identity\ndocuments; or\n\n(vi) if the engagement is to involve the provision of sexual\nservices—that fact, or the nature of sexual services to be\nprovided (for example, whether those services will\nrequire the victim to have unprotected sex).\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 9 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 7 years.",
      "skos:definition": "(ii) the extent to which the victim will be free to cease\nproviding the labour or services; or\n\n(iii) the extent to which the victim will be free to leave his or\nher place of residence; or\n\n(iv) if there is or will be a debt owed or claimed to be owed\nby the victim in connection with the engagement—the\nquantum, or the existence, of the debt owed or claimed\nto be owed; or\n\n(v) the fact that the engagement will involve exploitation,\nor the confiscation of the victim’s travel or identity\ndocuments; or\n\n(vi) if the engagement is to involve the provision of sexual\nservices—that fact, or the nature of sexual services to be\nprovided (for example, whether those services will\nrequire the victim to have unprotected sex).\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 9 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 7 years.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-3-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-3-logic-linearlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-3-logic-alleninterval-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6436fa46feedce7b68d7e3d17ab44d0a5cd521311ae7fb0818a1144c023bf6f0",
      "skos:note": "Restricts certain employment practices."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-2013-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2013 No. 6, 2013            9",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(ii) the extent to which the victim will be free to cease\nproviding the labour or services; or\n\n(iii) the extent to which the victim will be free to leave his or\nher place of residence; or\n\n(iv) if there is or will be a debt owed or claimed to be owed\nby the victim in connection with the engagement—the\nquantum, or the existence, of the debt owed or claimed\nto be owed; or\n\n(v) the fact that the engagement will involve exploitation,\nor the confiscation of the victim’s travel or identity\ndocuments; or\n\n(vi) if the engagement is to involve the provision of sexual\nservices—that fact, or the nature of sexual services to be\nprovided (for example, whether those services will\nrequire the victim to have unprotected sex).\nPenalty:\n\n(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—\nimprisonment for 9 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 7 years."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits exploitation and confiscation of travel or identity documents.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(ii) the extent to which the victim will be free to cease providing the labour or services;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No exploitation or confiscation allowed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-3-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits provision of sexual services requiring unprotected sex.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(vi) if the engagement is to involve the provision of sexual services—that fact, or the nature of sexual services to be provided (for example, whether those services will require the victim to have unprotected sex).",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No unprotected sex required."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-3-logic-linearlogic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Imply",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Implies imprisonment for specific terms based on offense severity.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) in the case of an aggravated offence (see section 270.8)—",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Penalty depends on offense severity."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-3-logic-alleninterval-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlap",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Overlaps with other provisions regarding employment practices and penalties.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) in any other case—",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Other cases have different penalties."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "270 7A  Definition of forced marriage",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, a marriage is a forced marriage\nif, because of the use of coercion, threat or deception, one party to\nthe marriage (the victim) entered into the marriage without freely\nand fully consenting.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), marriage includes the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) a registered relationship within the meaning of section 2E of\nthe Acts Interpretation Act 1901;\n\n(b) a marriage recognised under a law of a foreign country;\n\n(c) a relationship registered (however that process is described)\nunder a law of a foreign country, if the relationship is of the\nsame, or a similar, type as any registered relationship within\nthe meaning of section 2E of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901;\n\n(d) a marriage (including a relationship or marriage mentioned in\nparagraph (a), (b) or (c)) that is void, invalid, or not\nrecognised by law, for any reason, including the following:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Criminal Code amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, a marriage is a forced marriage\nif, because of the use of coercion, threat or deception, one party to\nthe marriage (the victim) entered into the marriage without freely\nand fully consenting.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), marriage includes the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) a registered relationship within the meaning of section 2E of\nthe Acts Interpretation Act 1901;\n\n(b) a marriage recognised under a law of a foreign country;\n\n(c) a relationship registered (however that process is described)\nunder a law of a foreign country, if the relationship is of the\nsame, or a similar, type as any registered relationship within\nthe meaning of section 2E of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901;\n\n(d) a marriage (including a relationship or marriage mentioned in\nparagraph (a), (b) or (c)) that is void, invalid, or not\nrecognised by law, for any reason, including the following:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Criminal Code amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-8-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-8-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8a3fcafba78db5f2dc7605151918f991b6fa812efde9071b84aa8bd845f8cc73"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "270 7A  Definition of forced marriage",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, a marriage is a forced marriage\nif, because of the use of coercion, threat or deception, one party to\nthe marriage (the victim) entered into the marriage without freely\nand fully consenting.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), marriage includes the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) a registered relationship within the meaning of section 2E of\nthe Acts Interpretation Act 1901;\n\n(b) a marriage recognised under a law of a foreign country;\n\n(c) a relationship registered (however that process is described)\nunder a law of a foreign country, if the relationship is of the\nsame, or a similar, type as any registered relationship within\nthe meaning of section 2E of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901;\n\n(d) a marriage (including a relationship or marriage mentioned in\nparagraph (a), (b) or (c)) that is void, invalid, or not\nrecognised by law, for any reason, including the following:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Criminal Code amendments"
    },
