      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Subsection (2) does not apply if the person has a reasonable excuse.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The defendant must provide evidence of a reasonable excuse during this interval."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "270 8  Slavery-like offences—aggravated offences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-270-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, a slavery-like offence committed\nby a person (the offender) against another person (the victim) is an\naggravated offence if any of the following applies:\n\n(a) the victim is under 18;\n\n(b) the offender, in committing the offence, subjects the victim to\ncruel, inhuman or degrading treatment;\n\n(c) the offender, in committing the offence:\n\n(i) engages in conduct that gives rise to a danger of death\nor serious harm to the victim or another person; and\n\n(ii) is reckless as to that danger.\n\n(2) If the prosecution intends to prove an aggravated offence, the\ncharge must allege the relevant aggravated offence.\n\n(3) If, on a trial for an aggravated offence, the trier of fact is not\nsatisfied that the defendant is guilty of the aggravated offence, but\nis otherwise satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the\ncorresponding slavery-like offence, it may find the defendant not\nguilty of the aggravated offence, but guilty of the corresponding\nslavery-like offence.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) only applies if the defendant has been afforded\nprocedural fairness in relation to the finding of guilt for the\ncorresponding slavery-like offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Division, a slavery-like offence committed\nby a person (the offender) against another person (the victim) is an\naggravated offence if any of the following applies:\n\n(a) the victim is under 18;\n\n(b) the offender, in committing the offence, subjects the victim to\ncruel, inhuman or degrading treatment;\n\n(c) the offender, in committing the offence:\n\n(i) engages in conduct that gives rise to a danger of death\nor serious harm to the victim or another person; and\n\n(ii) is reckless as to that danger.\n\n(2) If the prosecution intends to prove an aggravated offence, the\ncharge must allege the relevant aggravated offence.\n\n(3) If, on a trial for an aggravated offence, the trier of fact is not\nsatisfied that the defendant is guilty of the aggravated offence, but\nis otherwise satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the\ncorresponding slavery-like offence, it may find the defendant not\nguilty of the aggravated offence, but guilty of the corresponding\nslavery-like offence.\n\n(4) Subsection (3) only applies if the defendant has been afforded\nprocedural fairness in relation to the finding of guilt for the\ncorresponding slavery-like offence.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-10-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-10-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-10-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-270-10-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a26f99d0873244832eb6afd2586dc40e196cfe3541fa07444422e78379607a6a"
    },
    {
