    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "271 7A  Removal of organs contrary to this Subdivision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-271-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "The removal of a person’s organ is contrary to this Subdivision if:\n\n(a) the removal, or entering into an agreement for the removal,\nwould be contrary to the law of the State or Territory where it\nis, or is to be, carried out; or\n\n(b) neither the victim, nor the victim’s guardian, consents to the\nremoval, and it would not meet a medical or therapeutic need\nof the victim.",
      "skos:definition": "The removal of a person’s organ is contrary to this Subdivision if:\n\n(a) the removal, or entering into an agreement for the removal,\nwould be contrary to the law of the State or Territory where it\nis, or is to be, carried out; or\n\n(b) neither the victim, nor the victim’s guardian, consents to the\nremoval, and it would not meet a medical or therapeutic need\nof the victim.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6b47f66f050f753ab061029d1f12c240996a6c45859568e40ceaf46b8efa76a7",
      "skos:note": "Removal of organs contrary to this Subdivision is prohibited if certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-271-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "271 7A  Removal of organs contrary to this Subdivision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "The removal of a person’s organ is contrary to this Subdivision if:\n\n(a) the removal, or entering into an agreement for the removal,\nwould be contrary to the law of the State or Territory where it\nis, or is to be, carried out; or\n\n(b) neither the victim, nor the victim’s guardian, consents to the\nremoval, and it would not meet a medical or therapeutic need\nof the victim."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of organ removal",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Removal is contrary to the law of the State or Territory",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Prohibited"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "271 7B  Offence of organ trafficking—entry into and exit from",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-271-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "Australia\nEntry into Australia\n\n(1) A person (the offender) commits an offence of organ trafficking if:\n\n(a) the offender engages in conduct consisting of the\norganisation or facilitation of the entry or proposed entry, or\nthe receipt, of another person (the victim) into Australia; and\n\n(b) the offender is reckless as to whether the conduct will result\nin the removal of an organ of the victim contrary to this\nSubdivision, by the offender or another person, after or in the\ncourse of that entry or receipt.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nCriminal Code amendments  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act",
      "skos:definition": "Australia\nEntry into Australia\n\n(1) A person (the offender) commits an offence of organ trafficking if:\n\n(a) the offender engages in conduct consisting of the\norganisation or facilitation of the entry or proposed entry, or\nthe receipt, of another person (the victim) into Australia; and\n\n(b) the offender is reckless as to whether the conduct will result\nin the removal of an organ of the victim contrary to this\nSubdivision, by the offender or another person, after or in the\ncourse of that entry or receipt.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nCriminal Code amendments  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "634c6b97e7346d8a87582c2f527cb74fb4349e965c39aa2dba8d0697ef033ecf",
      "skos:note": "Offence of organ trafficking—entry into and exit from Australia"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-271-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "271 7B  Offence of organ trafficking—entry into and exit from",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "Australia\nEntry into Australia\n\n(1) A person (the offender) commits an offence of organ trafficking if:\n\n(a) the offender engages in conduct consisting of the\norganisation or facilitation of the entry or proposed entry, or\nthe receipt, of another person (the victim) into Australia; and\n\n(b) the offender is reckless as to whether the conduct will result\nin the removal of an organ of the victim contrary to this\nSubdivision, by the offender or another person, after or in the\ncourse of that entry or receipt.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nCriminal Code amendments  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits organ trafficking",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Offender commits an offence of organ trafficking",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Offence of organ trafficking is prohibited"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2013 No. 6, 2013            17",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-2013-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 years.\nNote:\nFor when the removal of an organ is contrary to this Subdivision, see\nsection 271.7A.\nExit from Australia\n\n(2) A person (the offender) commits an offence of organ trafficking if:\n\n(a) the offender engages in conduct consisting of the\norganisation or facilitation of the exit or proposed exit of\nanother person (the victim) from Australia; and\n\n(b) the offender is reckless as to whether the conduct will result\nin the removal of an organ of the victim contrary to this\nSubdivision, by the offender or another person, after or in the\ncourse of that exit.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 years.\nNote:\nFor when the removal of an organ is contrary to this Subdivision, see\nsection 271.7A.",
      "skos:definition": "Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 years.\nNote:\nFor when the removal of an organ is contrary to this Subdivision, see\nsection 271.7A.\nExit from Australia\n\n(2) A person (the offender) commits an offence of organ trafficking if:\n\n(a) the offender engages in conduct consisting of the\norganisation or facilitation of the exit or proposed exit of\nanother person (the victim) from Australia; and\n\n(b) the offender is reckless as to whether the conduct will result\nin the removal of an organ of the victim contrary to this\nSubdivision, by the offender or another person, after or in the\ncourse of that exit.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 years.\nNote:\nFor when the removal of an organ is contrary to this Subdivision, see\nsection 271.7A.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8b5f111355a725776fbfdd8180ec28bf6644ba028f7811fc82fbdb394fa9ebf8",
      "skos:note": "Organ trafficking is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-2013-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2013 No. 6, 2013            17",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 years.\nNote:\nFor when the removal of an organ is contrary to this Subdivision, see\nsection 271.7A.\nExit from Australia\n\n(2) A person (the offender) commits an offence of organ trafficking if:\n\n(a) the offender engages in conduct consisting of the\norganisation or facilitation of the exit or proposed exit of\nanother person (the victim) from Australia; and\n\n(b) the offender is reckless as to whether the conduct will result\nin the removal of an organ of the victim contrary to this\nSubdivision, by the offender or another person, after or in the\ncourse of that exit.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 years.\nNote:\nFor when the removal of an organ is contrary to this Subdivision, see\nsection 271.7A."
    },
    {
