      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the offender) commits an aggravated offence of organ\ntrafficking if the offender commits an offence of organ trafficking\nin relation to another person (the victim) and any of the following\napplies:\n\n(a) the victim is under 18;\n\n(b) the offender commits the offence intending that an organ of\nthe victim will be removed contrary to this Subdivision,\neither by the offender or another person:\n\n(i) if the offence of organ trafficking is an offence against\nsubsection 271.7B(1)—after or in the course of entry\ninto Australia; or\n\n(ii) if the offence of organ trafficking is an offence against\nsubsection 271.7B(2)—after or in the course of exit\nfrom Australia;\n\n(c) the offender, in committing the offence, subjects the victim to\ncruel, inhuman or degrading treatment;\n\n(d) the offender, in committing the offence:\n\n(i) engages in conduct that gives rise to a danger of death\nor serious harm to the victim or another person; and\n\n(ii) is reckless as to that danger.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Criminal Code amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person (the offender) commits an aggravated offence of organ\ntrafficking if the offender commits an offence of organ trafficking\nin relation to another person (the victim) and any of the following\napplies:\n\n(a) the victim is under 18;\n\n(b) the offender commits the offence intending that an organ of\nthe victim will be removed contrary to this Subdivision,\neither by the offender or another person:\n\n(i) if the offence of organ trafficking is an offence against\nsubsection 271.7B(1)—after or in the course of entry\ninto Australia; or\n\n(ii) if the offence of organ trafficking is an offence against\nsubsection 271.7B(2)—after or in the course of exit\nfrom Australia;\n\n(c) the offender, in committing the offence, subjects the victim to\ncruel, inhuman or degrading treatment;\n\n(d) the offender, in committing the offence:\n\n(i) engages in conduct that gives rise to a danger of death\nor serious harm to the victim or another person; and\n\n(ii) is reckless as to that danger.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Criminal Code amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-6-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-6-logic-linearlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-6-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d81a750c9af49cefd37130d5e510fb2fa345d1623088adb5e8f47c36bcf925e2",
      "skos:note": "Aggravated offence of organ trafficking if victim is under 18 or subjected to cruel treatment."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-271-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "271 7C  Organ trafficking—aggravated offence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the offender) commits an aggravated offence of organ\ntrafficking if the offender commits an offence of organ trafficking\nin relation to another person (the victim) and any of the following\napplies:\n\n(a) the victim is under 18;\n\n(b) the offender commits the offence intending that an organ of\nthe victim will be removed contrary to this Subdivision,\neither by the offender or another person:\n\n(i) if the offence of organ trafficking is an offence against\nsubsection 271.7B(1)—after or in the course of entry\ninto Australia; or\n\n(ii) if the offence of organ trafficking is an offence against\nsubsection 271.7B(2)—after or in the course of exit\nfrom Australia;\n\n(c) the offender, in committing the offence, subjects the victim to\ncruel, inhuman or degrading treatment;\n\n(d) the offender, in committing the offence:\n\n(i) engages in conduct that gives rise to a danger of death\nor serious harm to the victim or another person; and\n\n(ii) is reckless as to that danger.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nSchedule 1  Criminal Code amendments"
    },
