    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-18-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-18-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "Penalty:\n\n(a) if this subsection applies because the victim is under 18—\nimprisonment for 25 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 20 years.\nNote:\nFor when the removal of an organ is contrary to this Subdivision, see\nsection 271.7A.\n\n(2) If, on a trial for an offence against this section, the court, or if the\ntrial is before a jury, the jury, is not satisfied that the defendant is\nguilty of the aggravated offence, but is satisfied that he or she is\nguilty of an offence against section 271.7B, it may find the\ndefendant not guilty of the aggravated offence but guilty of an\noffence against that section.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) only applies if the defendant has been afforded\nprocedural fairness in relation to the finding of guilt for the offence\nagainst section 271.7B.\nNote:\nSection 271.7B provides for offences of organ trafficking.",
      "skos:definition": "Penalty:\n\n(a) if this subsection applies because the victim is under 18—\nimprisonment for 25 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 20 years.\nNote:\nFor when the removal of an organ is contrary to this Subdivision, see\nsection 271.7A.\n\n(2) If, on a trial for an offence against this section, the court, or if the\ntrial is before a jury, the jury, is not satisfied that the defendant is\nguilty of the aggravated offence, but is satisfied that he or she is\nguilty of an offence against section 271.7B, it may find the\ndefendant not guilty of the aggravated offence but guilty of an\noffence against that section.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) only applies if the defendant has been afforded\nprocedural fairness in relation to the finding of guilt for the offence\nagainst section 271.7B.\nNote:\nSection 271.7B provides for offences of organ trafficking.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-18-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-18-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f3a4e9a6c5418e5475c7d399dce6003aefd1a33655d155cc7ed669adec1371e7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-18-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "Penalty:\n\n(a) if this subsection applies because the victim is under 18—\nimprisonment for 25 years; or\n\n(b) in any other case—imprisonment for 20 years.\nNote:\nFor when the removal of an organ is contrary to this Subdivision, see\nsection 271.7A.\n\n(2) If, on a trial for an offence against this section, the court, or if the\ntrial is before a jury, the jury, is not satisfied that the defendant is\nguilty of the aggravated offence, but is satisfied that he or she is\nguilty of an offence against section 271.7B, it may find the\ndefendant not guilty of the aggravated offence but guilty of an\noffence against that section.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) only applies if the defendant has been afforded\nprocedural fairness in relation to the finding of guilt for the offence\nagainst section 271.7B.\nNote:\nSection 271.7B provides for offences of organ trafficking."
    },
