    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "271 7G  Harbouring a victim—aggravated offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-271-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the offender) commits an aggravated offence of\nharbouring a victim if:\n\n(a) the offender commits an offence of harbouring a victim in\nrelation to another person (the victim); and\n\n(b) the victim is under 18.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.\n\n(2) If, on a trial for an offence against this section, the trier of fact is\nnot satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the aggravated offence,\nbut is satisfied that the defendant is guilty of an offence against\nsection 271.7F, it may find the defendant not guilty of the\naggravated offence, but guilty of an offence against that section.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) only applies if the defendant has been afforded\nprocedural fairness in relation to the finding of guilt for the offence\nagainst section 271.7F.\nNote:\nSection 271.7F provides for the offence of harbouring a victim.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person (the offender) commits an aggravated offence of\nharbouring a victim if:\n\n(a) the offender commits an offence of harbouring a victim in\nrelation to another person (the victim); and\n\n(b) the victim is under 18.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.\n\n(2) If, on a trial for an offence against this section, the trier of fact is\nnot satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the aggravated offence,\nbut is satisfied that the defendant is guilty of an offence against\nsection 271.7F, it may find the defendant not guilty of the\naggravated offence, but guilty of an offence against that section.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) only applies if the defendant has been afforded\nprocedural fairness in relation to the finding of guilt for the offence\nagainst section 271.7F.\nNote:\nSection 271.7F provides for the offence of harbouring a victim.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-10-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-10-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-10-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bcda7723ee8ab187c9efe4e9bedcb11c945cc4c99bea495056111d6bc97cf641"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-271-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "271 7G  Harbouring a victim—aggravated offence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the offender) commits an aggravated offence of\nharbouring a victim if:\n\n(a) the offender commits an offence of harbouring a victim in\nrelation to another person (the victim); and\n\n(b) the victim is under 18.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.\n\n(2) If, on a trial for an offence against this section, the trier of fact is\nnot satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the aggravated offence,\nbut is satisfied that the defendant is guilty of an offence against\nsection 271.7F, it may find the defendant not guilty of the\naggravated offence, but guilty of an offence against that section.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) only applies if the defendant has been afforded\nprocedural fairness in relation to the finding of guilt for the offence\nagainst section 271.7F.\nNote:\nSection 271.7F provides for the offence of harbouring a victim."
    },
