    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "271 9  Debt bondage—aggravated offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-271-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the offender) commits an offence of aggravated debt\nbondage if the offender commits an offence of debt bondage in\nrelation to another person (the victim) and any of the following\napplies:\n\n(a) the victim is under 18;\n\n(b) the offender, in committing the offence, subjects the victim to\ncruel, inhuman or degrading treatment;\n\n(c) the offender, in committing the offence:\n\n(i) engages in conduct that gives rise to a danger of death\nor serious harm to the victim or another person; and\n\n(ii) is reckless as to that danger.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.\n\n(2) If, on a trial for an offence against this section, the trier of fact is\nnot satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the aggravated offence,\nbut is satisfied that the defendant is guilty of an offence against\nsection 271.8, it may find the defendant not guilty of the\naggravated offence, but guilty of an offence against that section.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) only applies if the defendant has been afforded\nprocedural fairness in relation to the finding of guilt for the offence\nagainst section 271.8.\nNote:\nSection 271.8 provides for the offence of debt bondage.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person (the offender) commits an offence of aggravated debt\nbondage if the offender commits an offence of debt bondage in\nrelation to another person (the victim) and any of the following\napplies:\n\n(a) the victim is under 18;\n\n(b) the offender, in committing the offence, subjects the victim to\ncruel, inhuman or degrading treatment;\n\n(c) the offender, in committing the offence:\n\n(i) engages in conduct that gives rise to a danger of death\nor serious harm to the victim or another person; and\n\n(ii) is reckless as to that danger.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.\n\n(2) If, on a trial for an offence against this section, the trier of fact is\nnot satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the aggravated offence,\nbut is satisfied that the defendant is guilty of an offence against\nsection 271.8, it may find the defendant not guilty of the\naggravated offence, but guilty of an offence against that section.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) only applies if the defendant has been afforded\nprocedural fairness in relation to the finding of guilt for the offence\nagainst section 271.8.\nNote:\nSection 271.8 provides for the offence of debt bondage.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-11-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-11-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-11-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9d81596a5526c2bae0cf6e6c20f04203745985e81988b5e396d4f25a48e87691"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-271-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "271 9  Debt bondage—aggravated offence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the offender) commits an offence of aggravated debt\nbondage if the offender commits an offence of debt bondage in\nrelation to another person (the victim) and any of the following\napplies:\n\n(a) the victim is under 18;\n\n(b) the offender, in committing the offence, subjects the victim to\ncruel, inhuman or degrading treatment;\n\n(c) the offender, in committing the offence:\n\n(i) engages in conduct that gives rise to a danger of death\nor serious harm to the victim or another person; and\n\n(ii) is reckless as to that danger.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years.\n\n(2) If, on a trial for an offence against this section, the trier of fact is\nnot satisfied that the defendant is guilty of the aggravated offence,\nbut is satisfied that the defendant is guilty of an offence against\nsection 271.8, it may find the defendant not guilty of the\naggravated offence, but guilty of an offence against that section.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) only applies if the defendant has been afforded\nprocedural fairness in relation to the finding of guilt for the offence\nagainst section 271.8.\nNote:\nSection 271.8 provides for the offence of debt bondage."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-11-ss-1",
