    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-15",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "271 11A  Offences against Division 271—relevant evidence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-271-15"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of proceedings for an offence against this\nDivision, the trier of fact may have regard to any of the matters\ncovered by subsection (2) in determining whether, in relation to a\nperson (the alleged victim) against whom the offence is alleged to\nhave been committed:\n\n(a) in the case of an offence against Subdivision B or BB—the\nalleged victim has been coerced, threatened or deceived; or\n\n(b) in the case of an offence against Subdivision BA—the\nalleged victim, or the alleged victim’s guardian, has\nconsented to the removal of an organ of the alleged victim; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nCriminal Code amendments  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of proceedings for an offence against this\nDivision, the trier of fact may have regard to any of the matters\ncovered by subsection (2) in determining whether, in relation to a\nperson (the alleged victim) against whom the offence is alleged to\nhave been committed:\n\n(a) in the case of an offence against Subdivision B or BB—the\nalleged victim has been coerced, threatened or deceived; or\n\n(b) in the case of an offence against Subdivision BA—the\nalleged victim, or the alleged victim’s guardian, has\nconsented to the removal of an organ of the alleged victim; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nCriminal Code amendments  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-15-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-15-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "66e997f3a7fa14ebf92d6d8099f1cfa1d48cfb135b944f335aaf522b2aaee5b4",
      "skos:note": "Relevant evidence for proceedings against an offence against Division 271—coercion, threat, or deception"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-271-15",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "271 11A  Offences against Division 271—relevant evidence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of proceedings for an offence against this\nDivision, the trier of fact may have regard to any of the matters\ncovered by subsection (2) in determining whether, in relation to a\nperson (the alleged victim) against whom the offence is alleged to\nhave been committed:\n\n(a) in the case of an offence against Subdivision B or BB—the\nalleged victim has been coerced, threatened or deceived; or\n\n(b) in the case of an offence against Subdivision BA—the\nalleged victim, or the alleged victim’s guardian, has\nconsented to the removal of an organ of the alleged victim; or\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00006\n\nCriminal Code amendments  Schedule 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Slavery, Slavery-like Conditions and People Trafficking) Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-15-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-15"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-271-15-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has",
      "cml:logicSummary": "State has obligation to provide relevant evidence",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2013 No. 6, 2013            23",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-2013-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(c) in the case of an offence against Subdivision C—another\nperson has caused the alleged victim to enter into debt\nbondage.\n\n(2) The following matters are covered by this subsection:\n\n(a) the economic relationship between the alleged victim and the\nalleged offender;\n\n(b) the terms of any written or oral contract or agreement\nbetween the alleged victim and the alleged offender;\n\n(c) the personal circumstances of the alleged victim, including\nbut not limited to:\n\n(i) whether he or she is entitled to be in Australia under the\nMigration Act 1958; and\n\n(ii) his or her ability to speak, write and understand English\nor another language; and\n\n(iii) the extent of his or her social and physical dependence\non the alleged offender.\n\n(3) If subsection (1) applies in relation to the consent of an alleged\nvictim’s guardian to the removal of an organ of the alleged victim,\na reference in subsection (2) to the alleged victim is taken to\ninclude a reference to the alleged victim’s guardian.\n\n(4) Subsection (1) does not:\n\n(a) prevent the leading of any other evidence in the relevant\nproceedings; or\n\n(b) limit the manner in which evidence may be given or the\nadmissibility of evidence.",
      "skos:definition": "(c) in the case of an offence against Subdivision C—another\nperson has caused the alleged victim to enter into debt\nbondage.\n\n(2) The following matters are covered by this subsection:\n\n(a) the economic relationship between the alleged victim and the\nalleged offender;\n\n(b) the terms of any written or oral contract or agreement\nbetween the alleged victim and the alleged offender;\n\n(c) the personal circumstances of the alleged victim, including\nbut not limited to:\n\n(i) whether he or she is entitled to be in Australia under the\nMigration Act 1958; and\n\n(ii) his or her ability to speak, write and understand English\nor another language; and\n\n(iii) the extent of his or her social and physical dependence\non the alleged offender.\n\n(3) If subsection (1) applies in relation to the consent of an alleged\nvictim’s guardian to the removal of an organ of the alleged victim,\na reference in subsection (2) to the alleged victim is taken to\ninclude a reference to the alleged victim’s guardian.\n\n(4) Subsection (1) does not:\n\n(a) prevent the leading of any other evidence in the relevant\nproceedings; or\n\n(b) limit the manner in which evidence may be given or the\nadmissibility of evidence.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-10-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-10-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-10-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1c79b188fe2a22812b2c8fff1627c645aeaf226cff18208ce1f1a1c8aaa81f1c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-2013-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2013 No. 6, 2013            23",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "(c) in the case of an offence against Subdivision C—another\nperson has caused the alleged victim to enter into debt\nbondage.\n\n(2) The following matters are covered by this subsection:\n\n(a) the economic relationship between the alleged victim and the\nalleged offender;\n\n(b) the terms of any written or oral contract or agreement\nbetween the alleged victim and the alleged offender;\n\n(c) the personal circumstances of the alleged victim, including\nbut not limited to:\n\n(i) whether he or she is entitled to be in Australia under the\nMigration Act 1958; and\n\n(ii) his or her ability to speak, write and understand English\nor another language; and\n\n(iii) the extent of his or her social and physical dependence\non the alleged offender.\n\n(3) If subsection (1) applies in relation to the consent of an alleged\nvictim’s guardian to the removal of an organ of the alleged victim,\na reference in subsection (2) to the alleged victim is taken to\ninclude a reference to the alleged victim’s guardian.\n\n(4) Subsection (1) does not:\n\n(a) prevent the leading of any other evidence in the relevant\nproceedings; or\n\n(b) limit the manner in which evidence may be given or the\nadmissibility of evidence."
    },
    {
