      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Subsection (1) does not:\n\n(a) prevent the leading of any other evidence in the relevant\nproceedings; or\n\n(b) limit the manner in which evidence may be given or the\nadmissibility of evidence.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Subsection (1) does not:\n\n(a) prevent the leading of any other evidence in the relevant\nproceedings; or\n\n(b) limit the manner in which evidence may be given or the\nadmissibility of evidence.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-10"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-10-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-2013-10-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4ed9f4ff5c7ef6c2897cf7d1d73fc75fcc627d3795870b99641c775096be7f2d",
      "skos:note": "No leading of other evidence in proceedings is prevented."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-2013-10-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2013(4) No. 6, 2013            23",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Subsection (1) does not:\n\n(a) prevent the leading of any other evidence in the relevant\nproceedings; or\n\n(b) limit the manner in which evidence may be given or the\nadmissibility of evidence."
    },
