    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-51",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51 At the end of section 271.12 of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-51"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Division is not intended to\nexclude or limit the concurrent operation of any other law of the\nCommonwealth, or a law of a State or Territory, that makes:\n\n(a) an act or omission that is an offence against a provision of\nthis Division; or\n\n(b) a similar act or omission;\nan offence against the law of the Commonwealth, State or\nTerritory.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) applies even if the other law of the Commonwealth,\nor the law of the State or Territory, does any one or more of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) provides for a penalty for the offence that differs from the\npenalty provided for in this Division;\n\n(b) provides for a fault element in relation to the offence that\ndiffers from the fault elements applicable to the offence\nunder this Division;\n\n(c) provides for a defence in relation to the offence that differs\nfrom the defences applicable to the offence under this\nDivision.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Division is not intended to\nexclude or limit the concurrent operation of any other law of the\nCommonwealth, or a law of a State or Territory, that makes:\n\n(a) an act or omission that is an offence against a provision of\nthis Division; or\n\n(b) a similar act or omission;\nan offence against the law of the Commonwealth, State or\nTerritory.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) applies even if the other law of the Commonwealth,\nor the law of the State or Territory, does any one or more of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) provides for a penalty for the offence that differs from the\npenalty provided for in this Division;\n\n(b) provides for a fault element in relation to the offence that\ndiffers from the fault elements applicable to the offence\nunder this Division;\n\n(c) provides for a defence in relation to the offence that differs\nfrom the defences applicable to the offence under this\nDivision.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-51-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-51-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f552a1e79bdc74d313b3f0f000e309faa363c9b81f8db6b9d0fb2b41f0dcea48"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-51",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51 At the end of section 271.12 of the Criminal Code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Division is not intended to\nexclude or limit the concurrent operation of any other law of the\nCommonwealth, or a law of a State or Territory, that makes:\n\n(a) an act or omission that is an offence against a provision of\nthis Division; or\n\n(b) a similar act or omission;\nan offence against the law of the Commonwealth, State or\nTerritory.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) applies even if the other law of the Commonwealth,\nor the law of the State or Territory, does any one or more of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) provides for a penalty for the offence that differs from the\npenalty provided for in this Division;\n\n(b) provides for a fault element in relation to the offence that\ndiffers from the fault elements applicable to the offence\nunder this Division;\n\n(c) provides for a defence in relation to the offence that differs\nfrom the defences applicable to the offence under this\nDivision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-51-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51(2) At the end of section 271.12 of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-51-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2013a00006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2013a00006.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Division is not intended to\nexclude or limit the concurrent operation of any other law of the\nCommonwealth, or a law of a State or Territory, that makes:\n\n(a) an act or omission that is an offence against a provision of\nthis Division; or\n\n(b) a similar act or omission;\nan offence against the law of the Commonwealth, State or\nTerritory.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Division is not intended to\nexclude or limit the concurrent operation of any other law of the\nCommonwealth, or a law of a State or Territory, that makes:\n\n(a) an act or omission that is an offence against a provision of\nthis Division; or\n\n(b) a similar act or omission;\nan offence against the law of the Commonwealth, State or\nTerritory.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-51"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-51-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2013a00006-sch-1-sec-51-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7831dab8071d787926010a0781e02b6fd68755c6a93ab370aa3ca926f7bfe2f6",
      "skos:note": "No provision of this Division excludes or limits concurrent operation of other laws."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2013a00006#sch-1-sec-51-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51(2) At the end of section 271.12 of the Criminal Code",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Division is not intended to\nexclude or limit the concurrent operation of any other law of the\nCommonwealth, or a law of a State or Territory, that makes:\n\n(a) an act or omission that is an offence against a provision of\nthis Division; or\n\n(b) a similar act or omission;\nan offence against the law of the Commonwealth, State or\nTerritory."
    },
    {
